text(R/'media-plan/FATE2-S02/pronunciation.en.md','''# S02 pronunciation and spoken meaning review

Model/voice policy remains the owner-accepted Gemini3.8 Charon/Kore method. No new audio exists for this revised text. Written lesson text and captions are not replaced by pronunciation spellings.

Egyptian delivery uses the retained instructions: natural Cairene explanation for university students; Egyptian G, colloquial hamza where appropriate, stable warm timbre, complete connected passages. Appropriate shadda is manually placed; shadda does not substitute for actual recording/listening checks.

- MRL: Arabic speech uses «إم آر إل» after the full contextual meaning.
- ADI: Arabic speech uses «إيه دي آي» after the full contextual meaning.
- ملِّيجرام / كيلوجرام: do not collapse food mass, body mass, or the daily basis.
- المتبقّي، العيّنة، التعرّض، السُمِّيّة، محدَّد، الأوّل، نجمع كتل نفس المادة: retain real gemination where intended.
- المَيّه refers to water; ميّة in «نضرب في ميّة» and «عشرة في الميّة» is the numerical/percentage word. Keep context distinct.
- 0.20: صفر فاصلة اتنين;0.15: صفر فاصلة واحد خمسة;0.05: صفر فاصلة صفر خمسة;0.40: صفر فاصلة أربعة.
-0.030: صفر فاصلة صفر تلاتة;0.020: صفر فاصلة صفر اتنين;0.050: صفر فاصلة صفر خمسة.
-0.0010: صفر فاصلة صفر صفر واحد;0.010: صفر فاصلة صفر واحد. Insignificant final zero may be omitted in speech only; the displayed worked precision is retained.
-50kilograms: خمسين كيلوجرام;10percent: عشرة في الميّة.

Bounded actual-audio blind/reference review, invalid-review reconciliation and any necessary targeted repair still follow generation. Preserve original WAV/PCM before review; do not infer Egyptian accent acceptance from text marks or ASR matching.
''')
